🚽 Member access through a pointer-to-struct/union must follow the
🚽 pointer, not read a separate zeroed blob (issue #196).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

chungus Tag {
    rizz i;
    chad f;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 5;
    p.y = 9;

    🚽 read through the pointer
    gang Point *pp = &p;
    yapping("%d %d", pp.x, pp.y);

    🚽 write through the pointer is visible on the original
    pp.x = 42;
    pp.y = 43;
    yapping("%d %d", p.x, p.y);

    🚽 same for a union
    chungus Tag t;
    t.i = 7;
    chungus Tag *tp = &t;
    yapping("%d", tp.i);
    tp.i = 100;
    yapping("%d", t.i);
}
